Anonymous Function
Anonymous Functions are the predecessors of the Lambda Functions. Anonymous Function is made by removing the name from a regular function definition. An anonymous function is an expression that returns an object of functional type. It does not define a regular function.
Regular Function:
fun add1(a: Int, b: Int) = a + b
Anonymous Function:
val add2 = fun(a: Int, b: Int): Int {
    return a + b
}
We can use Single Expression and Regular Syntax when we define Anonymous Function. But not Generic Type Parameters and Default Arguements.
We need to use .invoke() to call a Function Type.
A Variable type can be inferred because Anonymous Function specify the type of result and Parameter.
